# Starts the in-session geometry loop, 200 % form (adr/0018 section 5.2 addendum four, item 2).
#
# WHAT IT DOES: copies window-loop.ps1 and window-rects-probe.ps1 onto the host, launches the
# loop detached (Start-Process, hidden) and writes \\tsclient\lab\window-loop-start.done before
# this connection ends. The loop then samples every visible top-level window's rectangles four
# times a second, HOST-LOCAL, and keeps doing so after xfreerdp exits -- which is the point:
# the window-rects probe can only measure the instant its own connection is up, and this covers
# the whole span from this disconnect, through the window-smoke run, to the probe's connection.
# Nothing on the host is changed beyond two files and the loop's output in the account's own
# macdows-lab directory: no registry, no service, no elevation, no port. The samples carry
# numbers, class names and process image names only -- never a window title (only its length and
# an 8-hex digest), never a user or computer name, never a path.
#
# OPERATOR ORDER. Consumed by relay.command through run-scenario.sh. The loop has to be running
# BEFORE the smoke run creates its windows, and a logoff destroys it, so it is started right
# after the opening logoff of a pair and never between the smoke run and the probe:
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay logoff-path         # open the pair on a clean session
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay window-loop-start-2x  # this job
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh smoke 2x-D-move-keep-about  # the run under study
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay window-rects-2x     # the probe
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay window-loop-collect-2x  # sentinel + carry the samples back
# Do NOT run `relay logoff-path` anywhere inside that sequence: logging off takes the loop's
# process with it along with the windows under study.
#
# WHY THE SCALE IS PINNED: the relay's connection declares its own TS_UD_CS_CORE
# desktopScaleFactor, and a client that joins a retained session with a DIFFERENT declared scale
# makes the server re-lay-out the session. This job's connection is one more client joining the
# session under study, so it declares the same 200 % the 2x smoke run will -- otherwise the act
# of starting the measurement would itself move the windows it is about to measure.
# deviceScaleFactor is deliberately NOT passed, so it stays at FreeRDP's unconditional 100 --
# product default D. relay.command admits /scale-desktop:<100-500> from its closed
# XFREERDP_EXTRA allowlist, so no relay change was needed for either form.
#
# Full path, not `||powershell`: the alias form resolves only against a published
# TSAppAllowList\Applications entry, and outside the matrix's Enforce window there is none (see
# jobs/server-snapshot.env for the full reasoning and the RAIL_EXEC_E_FILE_NOT_FOUND it earns).
#
# WHAT THE DONE MARKER SAYS. [loop-start] ends with head=<true|false>: whether the launcher saw
# the sampler's own [loop-head] line appear on the host within 3 s of the launch. head=false
# means the child never began executing (a staged copy that will not run, a leftover lock on the
# output, a launch the host refused after returning a handle) and is NOT evidence about
# surviving a disconnect; the host-local window-loop.stderr.txt holds the child's own complaint.
# The full four-way reading table is in jobs/window-loop-collect-*.env.
#
# OPERATOR STEP before every launch: remove the previous start marker, e.g.
#   rm -f .build/lab-runtime/share/window-loop-start.done
# run-scenario.sh deliberately never removes host-written *.done / *-out.txt (see stage_share),
# so a job the host refuses BEFORE the script starts would otherwise leave the previous pair's
# marker in place, looking like this pair's successful launch.
PROGRAM='C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe'
CMDARGS='-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\tsclient\lab\window-loop-start.ps1'
XFREERDP_EXTRA='/scale-desktop:200'
# Bound, and deliberately SHORT. relay.command polls until xfreerdp exits or this timeout kills
# it, so the connection is held for the whole window. This job only copies two small files and
# calls Start-Process, which returns immediately -- 30 s is the RAIL handshake plus that, with
# margin. It must not be long: the loop is already running and every extra second of this
# connection is a second of the timeline measured while an extra client is attached.
TIMEOUT=30
